f-target is intronic with 3 mismatches and low expression risk; no coding bystanders. No coding/exonic near-matches, so no safety concerns. Recommended as the safest guide with sufficient on-target activity.\n\n**g06 (rank 2, acceptable):**\nActivity score 0.64. The only annotated off-target is intergenic with 3 mismatches and low expression risk; no coding bystanders. No coding/exonic near-matches. Acceptable: safe profile but slightly lower on-target activity than g02.\n\n**g04 (rank 3, acceptable):**\nActivity score 0.59 (lowest among non-rejected). The only annotated off-target is intergenic with 4 mismatches and low expression risk; no coding bystanders. No coding/exonic near-matches. Acceptable but has the lowest on-target activity; safe.\n\n**g03 (rank 4, reject):**\nActivity score 0.74 (relatively high). However, the annotated off-target is a coding exon with only 2 mismatches (medium expression risk). By the frozen rule, a coding-exon hit with 2 or fewer mismatches triggers rejection. Trade-off: this guide has higher on-target activity than all recommended/acceptable guides, but is rejected because the exonic near-match is a safety concern. Risk class: high.\n\n**g01 (rank 5, reject):**\nActivity score 0.82 (highest overall). However, the annotated off-target is a coding exon with 1 mismatch and high expression risk; plus 1 coding bystander. Multiple rejection triggers. Risk class: critical (high-expression-risk hit and coding-exon hit with 1 mismatch). Trade-off: despite the best on-target activity, rejected due to severe safety concerns (exonic near-match in a highly expressed locus + bystander editing risk).\n\n**g05 (rank 6, reject):**\nActivity score 0.78. The annotated off-target is a coding exon with 1 mismatch and high expression risk; plus 2 coding bystanders. Multiple rejection triggers. Risk class: critical (high-expression-risk hit, 2 or more coding bystanders, and coding-exon hit with 1 mismatch). Trade-off: despite high on-target activity, rej